// =============================================================================
// Chora Guardrail Service (gRPC)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture-review-inputs-2026-05-07.md Tier 3 D11
//   + .claude/skills/ai-runtime-guardrails/SKILL.md
//   + .claude/rules/ddd-enforcement.md ("Risk-tiered guardrails per agent")
//
// Runtime guardrail evaluation for every LLM call (input AND output).
// Per-agent risk-tiered YAML config declares which tiers apply:
//   - REGEX: cheap baseline pattern match
//   - DLP: Cloud DLP scan (PII / financial / health detectors)
//   - MODEL_ARMOR: Cloud Model Armor toxicity + jailbreak + prompt-injection
//   - OUTPUT_VALIDATOR: structured output validators (JSON schema, citation
//     grounding, etc.)
//
// Evaluation flow:
//   Model Gateway → EvaluateInput  (pre-model)  → if PASS, call model
//                  → EvaluateOutput (post-model) → if PASS, return to caller
//
// Violations are logged to ContentPolicyViolationLog (chora_governance) by
// the Guardrail Service itself; this RPC contract does not require the caller
// to do the logging.
//
// Deployed in chora-489812 team-platform pool (separate from Model Broker).
// mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh; SPIFFE identity in mesh.
// =============================================================================

